      "title": "Quadratic nth Term, Functions & Iteration",
      "content": "<p><strong>Quadratic nth term:</strong> If second differences are constant = \\(2a\\), the sequence is \\(an^2 + bn + c\\). Find \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\) by subtracting \\(an^2\\) and finding the linear nth term of what remains.</p><p><strong>Functions:</strong> \\(fg(x)\\) means apply \\(g\\) first, then \\(f\\). Inverse \\(f^{-1}\\): swap \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), rearrange.</p><p><strong>Iteration:</strong> \\(x_{n+1} = g(x_n)\\). Substitute repeatedly from a starting value.</p>",
      "example": "<p><strong>Find the nth term of</strong> 3, 8, 15, 24, 35, ...</p><p>1st diff: 5, 7, 9, 11. 2nd diff: 2, so a=1.</p><p>Subtract \\(n^2\\): 2, 4, 6, 8 → linear: \\(2n\\).</p><p><strong>nth term = \\(n^2 + 2n\\)</strong></p>"
    },
